messages:
jenna_support: Customer (ACCT-93) reports 404s hitting our API after upgrading to @redwood/sdk@1.4.0. They say /models.list endpoint is missing and some param names changed — blocking prod. Pasting their minimal repro + error below.

devin_eng: thanks — can you drop the exact error and the client snippet?

jenna_support: paste from customer:
```ts
import Redwood from '@redwood/sdk';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
await client.models.list({ model: 'gpt-4-redwood' });
// => 404: endpoint not found: /v1/models.list
```
package.json: "@redwood/sdk": "1.4.0", "@redwood/api": "1.3.2"
logs: `HTTP 404 POST /v1/models.list - missing route`

nate_sdk: Ack. This matches a change we shipped in 1.4.0: we renamed some RPC paths/params in the TS client to align with the upcoming server-side v2 (models.list -> models.listAll, param model -> model_id). If the control plane is still on 1.3.x the client will call endpoints that don't exist and get 404.

mike_qa: repro checklist I ran locally: 1) npx create-node-app; 2) npm i @redwood/sdk@1.4.0; 3) run snippet above against staging (api v1.3.2) -> 404. Downgrade to 1.3.2 -> works. Verified.

sara_cs: customer needs a quick workaround now — recommend rollback to 1.3.2 while we patch? Also they are on a tight SLA.

nate_sdk: Agreed on rollback short-term. Workaround to send them: `npm install @redwood/sdk@1.3.2 --save` and restart service. Also we can give a small TS shim if they can’t change versions immediately:
```ts
// shim to map new->old params
const safeList = async (client, opts) => {
  const legacy = { model: opts.model_id ?? opts.model };
  try {
    return await client.call('models.list', legacy);
  } catch (e) {
    // if 404, retry with the legacy path
    if (e.status === 404) return await client.call('models.list', legacy);
    throw e;
  }
};
```

devin_eng: Plan proposal: publish 1.4.1 that 1) detects server capability/version on init 2) falls back to legacy endpoint/param names on 404 3) logs a visible warning advising upgrade when server supports new API. This keeps 1.4.x semantics but is safe with older control planes. Can we do a quick patch?

nate_sdk: I'll open PR with a small compatibility layer (detect via /v1/metadata or try a lightweight ping). ETA ~2h for PR + tests. Need approval to publish a patch release once QA signs off.

mike_qa: I'll add a smoke test matrix: client versions [1.3.2,1.4.0,1.4.1-rc] vs server [1.3.2, staging-v2]. Will validate fallback and that no extra auth regressions appear.

sara_cs: I provided the rollback instructions to the customer and asked if they'd like us to schedule a maintenance window for the reupgrade. They accepted rollback for now.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot: canary job started for @redwood/sdk 1.4.1-rc to staging (job id: canary-8792).

devin_eng: Nate — please tag me on the PR. Also update changelog to call out the compatibility layer and the root cause so customers see the note.

nate_sdk: Will do. PR -> #sdk-prs and I'll include repro snippet and the smoke test matrix.

jenna_support: Customer updated: rolled back to 1.3.2 and back in production. They asked for ETA for official fix — told them ~3 hours.

mike_qa: Quick note: add an integration test that asserts client logs a helpful error when mismatched (so support has consistent messaging).

devin_eng: :thumbsup: good triage. Follow up: open a short postmortem if this hits >1 customer or stays unresolved past EOD.

jenna_support: Closing loop with them now. Thanks team.
